build/

# Test binaries `odin test` leaves at the repository root.
#
# A clean run deletes its own binary; an *interrupted* one does not — and
# piping the output into `head`, or anything else that exits early, interrupts
# it. That is common enough while reading test output to be worth ignoring.
#
# The name is the package's last path component. Every entry is anchored with a
# leading slash so it can only ever match a file at the root, never the source
# directory of the same name — `shacl/memstore`, `shacl/kvstore`,
# `tests/guards`, `tests/readme`, `tests/w3c/harness` are all real packages, and
# an unanchored `memstore` would ignore one of them.
#
# Package `shacl` needs no entry: its binary would collide with the `shacl/`
# directory, so none is written. Do not add `/shacl` here — it would match the
# directory and ignore the whole core package.
/memstore
/kvstore
/guards
/readme
/harness

# Metis Ralph loop state -- per-session runtime state, not source
.claude/
